#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134901} :activity/id #uuid "fc007430-4cc9-562b-9192-4d3c9dccd500" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049312 :topic/id #uuid "eb826c2f-ae04-5de5-b6a6-7efcf7e974ae" :topic/math-academy-id 2201} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134901 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135151 :tutorial/content "If an $n\\!\\times \\!n$ matrix $A$ has an entire row or column of zeros, then its determinant is equal to zero.\n\nFor example, consider the matrix $A$ given below:\n\n![](images/6b/6bb8b64f7ed8730e641cdf88fc6fe7add40bc15061095c6b1f57c1b764b28feb.svg)\n\nThe second row consists of all zeros, and the asterisks ($\\ast$) may represent any number.\n\nLet's compute the determinant using the Laplace expansion across the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)^{2+1}(0)|\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}|+(-1)^{2+2}(0)|\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}|+(-1)^{2+3}(0)|\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+0+0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that it doesn't matter what numbers are represented by the asterisks ($\\ast$). Each cofactor is multiplied by zero, so the final result must be zero." :tutorial/id #uuid "cee0a552-60f2-5785-a506-63bd053364c7" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6888 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "b68428f5-f5bb-5090-b7f9-4971dc931914" :step/math-academy-id 41745 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134902}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134902 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135152 :tutorial/content "Now, suppose a matrix has no zero rows but it has two identical rows:\n\n![](images/74/7477781b618ec384b1638d01707acf545e7d9882ffca5bbc0efde4e224b04308.svg)\n\nWe can subtract the $1$st row from the $3$rd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this operation does not change the determinant, we get $\\det(A) = \\det(B).$ Furthermore, as $B$ contains a zero row, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = \\det(B) = 0.\n$$\n\nNotice that we can use this method with columns too. Therefore, we have the following property:\n\n*If a square matrix has at least two identical rows/columns, its determinant equals zero.*" :tutorial/id #uuid "6813d49e-3908-5735-8196-8e1aad5a14e6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6889 :tutorial/title "Determinants with Identical Rows or Identical Columns"} :step/id #uuid "e105e6ae-64b8-5812-85e8-b5c3ef7b6c7d" :step/math-academy-id 41746 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134903}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134903 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133911 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133466 :question/id #uuid "bb2795c3-6359-50d8-9531-1e9dfae7a2ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-10994"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048462} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049159}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134395} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134408} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272009} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329700} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351408} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400867} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420351} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420352} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427636}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"} :step/id #uuid "f2a27f52-c605-5d01-84c1-49531f59d922" :step/math-academy-id 41747 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134904}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134904 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135153 :tutorial/content "Now, suppose a matrix has no zero rows and no identical rows but it has two proportional rows:\n\n![](images/81/8181d36ff1378310744b0d74f42f2934eb1e41053f45ecfeacf0c813abe994df.svg)\n\nWe can add three times the $1$st row to the $3$rd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this operation does not change the determinant, we get $\\det(A) = \\det(B).$ Furthermore, as $B$ contains a zero row, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = \\det(B) = 0.\n$$\n\nNotice that we can use this method with columns too. Therefore, we have the following property:\n\n*If a square matrix has at least two proportional rows/columns, its determinant equals zero.*" :tutorial/id #uuid "fe83e8c9-948a-596f-a2d9-c2ae2fe4f335" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6890 :tutorial/title "Determinants with Proportional Rows/Columns"} :step/id #uuid "23e26677-bdeb-5a45-a6d3-4a8d02a72732" :step/math-academy-id 41750 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134905}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134905 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133467 :question/id #uuid "dc780837-b763-5ba9-981a-2373afcb524a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10995"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134394} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134407} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272011} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329654} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351409} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402861} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402868} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411852} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415475} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415477} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415478}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"} :step/id #uuid "93111f5e-5fd2-5a5b-81b1-27969a9b5d1d" :step/math-academy-id 41751 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134906}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134906 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135154 :tutorial/content "In conclusion, if an $n\\!\\times \\!n$ matrix $A$ satisfies any one of the following conditions, then $\\det(A)=0.$\n\n- $A$ has a zero row/column\n\n- $A$ has two identical rows/columns\n\n- $A$ has two proportional rows/columns\n\n- $A$ has a row/column that is a linear combination of other rows/columns\n\nNotice that condition IV encompasses each of the conditions I, II, and III. If we have a zero row/column, two identical rows/columns, or proportional rows/columns, then the rows/columns form a linearly dependent set of vectors. \nIn turn, this means that one of the rows/columns is a linear combination of other rows/columns.\n\n**Watch out!** While all of the above conditions are *sufficient* to conclude that $\\det(A)=0,$ only condition IV is *necessary* to conclude that $\\det(A)=0.$ \nIn other words, if we have a matrix $A$ with $\\det(A)=0,$ then conditions I, II, and III may or may not be satisfied, while condition IV *must* be satisfied. \n\nSo, we have the following theorem:\n\n*$\\det(A)=0$ if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nFinally, note also that in the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix *only*, statements III and IV mean the same thing." :tutorial/id #uuid "9d8b0323-170c-5a60-b372-1a258c4848cc" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6891 :tutorial/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero"} :step/id #uuid "4aec093b-050b-5263-9ef2-c875455b8c07" :step/math-academy-id 41754 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134908}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134907 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133468 :question/id #uuid "33ca37e5-c598-52a2-861f-2d5bfa6fd571" :question/math-academy-id "e-10996"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134393} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134414} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272012} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272013} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329652} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329653} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329699} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351410} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415476} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415479} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420353}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"} :step/id #uuid "81571aa7-ce3d-5713-bf67-a49538fee0ef" :step/math-academy-id 41755} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134908 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135155 :tutorial/content "Geometrically, the absolute value of an $n \\times n$ determinant can be interpreted as the volume of the $n$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the columns of the determinant. \n\nFor example:\n\n- Suppose the columns of a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ are ${\\color{black}\\mathbf{a}}, {\\color{black}\\mathbf{b}},$ and ${\\color{black}\\mathbf{c}}.$\n![](images/6e/6e046341b7a1b8f6760797f7db89a7e021a6ace6b5cdf28bd5217998cb450837.svg)\nThe $3$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the columns of $A$ is depicted below:\n\n![](images/25/2597b48a010607fca71c551dbce8e9e2bbeda47d0892a582347ae1cdf19f1bf6.png)\n\nThe volume $V$ of this parallelepiped equals the absolute value of the determinant of $A{:}$\n\n$$\nV = \\left|\\det(A)\\right|\n$$\n\n- Now suppose the columns of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ are ${\\color{black}\\mathbf{p}}$ and ${\\color{black}\\mathbf{q}}.$\n![](images/f5/f593c123eb081da0399e74c665325774758b48c5f086a7475b959905e1de2763.svg)\nThe $2$-dimensional parallelepiped (i.e., the parallelogram) spanned by vectors $\\mathbf{p}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ is shown below:\n\n![](images/4a/4af1971404b188df75bb3d62d47ac95340c5e1791066e5358370d743230baa45.png)\n\nThe two-dimensional volume $V$ (i.e., the area) of this parallelepiped equals the absolute value of the determinant of $B{:}$\n\n$$\nV = \\left|\\det(B)\\right|\n$$\n\n- In general, the absolute value of the determinant of an $n\\times n$ matrix $M$ gives the $n$-dimensional volume of the parallelepiped spanned by the columns of $M.$\n\nIn this lesson, we studied the following property:\n\n*$\\det(A) = 0$ if and only if one of the columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other columns of $A$.*\n\nWhat does this property mean in geometric terms?\n\nThe component $\\det(A) = 0$ implies that the $n$-dimensional parallelepiped formed by the columns of $A$ has zero volume. Conversely, when one of the columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other columns, it indicates that the corresponding parallelepiped possesses at most $n-1$ distinct dimensions. \n\nConsider the following examples:\n\n- In the case of a $3$-dimensional parallelepiped, if the vector $\\mathbf{c}$ is a linear combination of the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\mathbf{c}$ lies within the plane containing $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$. In other words, the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$, $\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\mathbf{c}$ are coplanar. Consequently, we obtain a \"flat\" ($2$-dimensional) figure with a volume of $0$.\n\n- For the parallelogram example, if the vector $\\mathbf{q}$ is a linear combination of the vector $\\mathbf{p}$ (i.e., $\\mathbf{p}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ are proportional), then $\\mathbf{q}$ resides on the line containing vector $\\mathbf{p}$. In other words, the vectors $\\mathbf{p}$ and $\\mathbf{q}$ are collinear. This results in a $1$-dimensional object with a $2$-dimensional volume (i.e., area) of $0$." :tutorial/id #uuid "1f7191c6-60ca-5c44-befc-8dbad7779b08" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6893 :tutorial/title "Geometric Interpretation of a Zero Determinant"} :step/id #uuid "8c5dbeea-b2e4-5fe9-9d8c-98750164b70c" :step/math-academy-id 41766 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134907}}] :activity/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186134042}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046673} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415480} :activity/id #uuid "d3285aa6-5f09-548a-886c-a1acc2f7b8d6" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049312 :topic/id #uuid "eb826c2f-ae04-5de5-b6a6-7efcf7e974ae" :topic/math-academy-id 2201} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415480 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415477 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022ff781-0bb6-5222-8917-bb9fe088d40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} {:answer/id #uuid "68acb0f6-b335-5e47-b870-8fcc301ed02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415455} {:answer/id #uuid "a31adf10-60d1-51b5-9022-8cf1940c42be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415461} {:answer/id #uuid "ebaffa84-7e8a-5edc-8432-6adf9e5b2b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415465} {:answer/id #uuid "fae22a7a-c8b8-5a0b-bb2c-5bc815b3b48d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415467}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ec239f-8a57-5ead-b4ff-042aa539477e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d4554f29-f5fb-5556-852c-2f9d95422a4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42464" :question/problem "Find $5det(A)+7det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5det(A)+7det(B)=5\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 0=0.$"} :step/id #uuid "0922e6fb-1dc5-5a88-a985-bdf2643cb465" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415484}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415481 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d00532a-c12b-50b9-ad0b-b9f1fa474794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415449} {:answer/id #uuid "44173bde-0fab-57de-b1b3-22d94262de8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415452} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9c1118-9a19-54c3-9683-cf1248dd342b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415456} {:answer/id #uuid "7e862f84-0fe3-5f4e-8829-b54fb65649ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415457} {:answer/id #uuid "e9cd19d7-7290-5199-aa60-b1bc0b2d73b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415464}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415464} :answer-field/id #uuid "e80361a1-690f-54bf-a979-055f8bec64f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f8a11ae3-b740-5975-a251-a4796d69b742" :question/math-academy-id "q-43307" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ has a zero column\n- $A$ has two proportional rows\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nExpending across the $1$st column, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-2)+(1-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither a zero column nor two proportional rows.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} :step/id #uuid "73a434b3-1e72-5102-a3b4-f3e485e5088a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415482}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415482 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "045918a8-9cd8-5a07-b550-ae46024d9091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415446} {:answer/id #uuid "402ee237-56af-5ed0-b68b-15a4eb93a4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415451} {:answer/id #uuid "82c9a685-f3be-5652-9e92-444a23e21632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415458} {:answer/id #uuid "f5705fa2-288d-561a-9ae0-435e05884593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} {:answer/id #uuid "fff98d8e-e1e9-59ce-9f45-62d4096f2b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415469}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} :answer-field/id #uuid "3898e8c8-305f-5107-8e55-3fa0057b225c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "135c5d03-e391-5a5b-8227-7d54c7203318" :question/math-academy-id "q-140048" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n|A|=0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0=0\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"} :step/id #uuid "7fde0eea-1a95-5e36-bc1d-53171442da99"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415483 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415478 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1859d7c5-0d55-5273-a004-f8368886466b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415448} {:answer/id #uuid "4a61a420-d52d-5f1a-b48b-ade03dffdca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415453} {:answer/id #uuid "5fcc61bd-b9ee-5f9e-8558-651f8ea9c858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415454} {:answer/id #uuid "851dc3ec-467b-568b-a964-3b5e34b3527e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415459} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e4e722-717d-508c-a98d-112f70b09d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415463}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415463} :answer-field/id #uuid "f920ea7f-06a7-52e9-8586-d0e6b44af6b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e897ce2c-45dd-5cf3-9d25-ca84c0dd6ea8" :question/math-academy-id "q-42881" :question/problem "Find $3det(A)-det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3det(A)-det(B)=3\\cdot 6-0=18.$"} :step/id #uuid "8a73fe86-1dcc-5158-b5d0-cfa5bf0ca01e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415481}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415484 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415476 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "143f48c0-a939-5a4c-b987-afdbbefec79a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415447} {:answer/id #uuid "22066df8-6293-5194-a873-db4b694c6674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415450} {:answer/id #uuid "8e60b08a-cd17-575f-8815-735e23870208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415460} {:answer/id #uuid "b446fc5b-8c89-5d67-acf5-bbcf1be8249d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415462} {:answer/id #uuid "fe594f39-ea49-5697-a493-c1ebeaf625b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415468}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415450} :answer-field/id #uuid "44a7cadd-9704-50b9-80ee-df6bc66a727b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8d883981-f066-5218-a1bf-dd76574de46e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42469" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns\n- $A$ has identical rows\n- $A$ has a zero row" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "a995ede1-d1f3-53d5-97cb-aed29dce50f7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415483}}] :activity/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415444}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416116} :activity/id #uuid "9cb6054b-7ed5-5992-92b3-318764a5074c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049312 :topic/id #uuid "eb826c2f-ae04-5de5-b6a6-7efcf7e974ae" :topic/math-academy-id 2201} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416114 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415477 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022ff781-0bb6-5222-8917-bb9fe088d40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} {:answer/id #uuid "68acb0f6-b335-5e47-b870-8fcc301ed02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415455} {:answer/id #uuid "a31adf10-60d1-51b5-9022-8cf1940c42be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415461} {:answer/id #uuid "ebaffa84-7e8a-5edc-8432-6adf9e5b2b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415465} {:answer/id #uuid "fae22a7a-c8b8-5a0b-bb2c-5bc815b3b48d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415467}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ec239f-8a57-5ead-b4ff-042aa539477e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d4554f29-f5fb-5556-852c-2f9d95422a4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42464" :question/problem "Find $5det(A)+7det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5det(A)+7det(B)=5\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 0=0.$"} :step/id #uuid "21677cec-5329-5c17-ae68-e4ce9c1eced7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416118}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416115 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dc653f0-653a-51c8-9dde-134e1ea1131e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269831} {:answer/id #uuid "63282b85-24f9-5737-88f6-e544d18bead1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270146} {:answer/id #uuid "d283f88f-ed57-5c59-963f-f49777d28ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271122} {:answer/id #uuid "db49a675-ce1e-57fa-a849-aff9de416a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271188} {:answer/id #uuid "ecb23ab9-9422-51b8-8613-a343d4227bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271348}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271348} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfceea30-a8b2-5f6c-aa6e-a6e0d02cdbfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f60fdb9d-cf89-59bd-ad65-e9ec096b82df" :question/math-academy-id "q-140049" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ is a triangular matrix\n- $A$ does not have identical rows\n- $A$ does not have proportional columns" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 2=5\\ne 0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ is not a triangular matrix.\n\n- Statements II and III are true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\nHence, if $|A|\\ne 0$ then $A$ doesn't have proportional nor identical rows/columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} :step/id #uuid "5d4a636e-e59e-599e-aff6-d3384708bbf3"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416116 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329652 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005e27bf-cb54-5586-9f97-7b38aad175ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326938} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd6a87d-fb02-5806-ae65-64162e9cf218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327321} {:answer/id #uuid "8de5c3ae-cce3-5e55-9356-16f0393d6b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328163} {:answer/id #uuid "df2048ab-aecc-5672-ad82-8817a5b81317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328888} {:answer/id #uuid "f32e69b1-2499-5293-92c5-f46f9bacf57b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329059}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327321} :answer-field/id #uuid "49c4b9a1-7b38-5148-a1f8-07d819c935b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fffc6699-6d6e-50bb-8cc3-7d4f0e3f1d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-42460" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has a zero row\n- $A$ has two proportional columns\n- $A$ has two identical rows" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have a zero row.\n\n- $A$ has two proportional columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "72236d0c-8f54-552b-be75-f74f2ec50cbd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416114}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416117 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d00532a-c12b-50b9-ad0b-b9f1fa474794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415449} {:answer/id #uuid "44173bde-0fab-57de-b1b3-22d94262de8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415452} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9c1118-9a19-54c3-9683-cf1248dd342b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415456} {:answer/id #uuid "7e862f84-0fe3-5f4e-8829-b54fb65649ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415457} {:answer/id #uuid "e9cd19d7-7290-5199-aa60-b1bc0b2d73b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415464}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415464} :answer-field/id #uuid "e80361a1-690f-54bf-a979-055f8bec64f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f8a11ae3-b740-5975-a251-a4796d69b742" :question/math-academy-id "q-43307" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ has a zero column\n- $A$ has two proportional rows\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nExpending across the $1$st column, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-2)+(1-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither a zero column nor two proportional rows.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} :step/id #uuid "cd1aa3f6-63e2-5747-ab7a-9aca6a4ae1ae" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416115}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416118 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402861 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78b84216-c188-5769-a0cf-2f3c4b5d4fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402863} {:answer/id #uuid "47a2ba38-2156-5dd9-922d-70e7a9112796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402864} {:answer/id #uuid "bf232768-62b0-5a99-b6ae-c2f1d1ac4e96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402865} {:answer/id #uuid "5c171a58-43ca-5ac8-896f-be2e38df60c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402866} {:answer/id #uuid "75bb085b-9153-5df0-9e32-3ce23b5de8fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402867}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402863} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4619bd4-0fd6-5b0e-85d8-4d713cc4997e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b44f28c6-ca93-5246-be2b-1a2725d36e07" :question/math-academy-id "q-43057" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -6 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 8 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|A|=3\\cdot (-6)\\cdot 2=-36\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|C|=(-1)\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=-12\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ is equal to $0.$"} :step/id #uuid "dd405466-fc10-5821-904a-fe28c7027da8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416117}}] :activity/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416113}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427638} :activity/id #uuid "831bdc32-0d6c-55b8-aa0e-17d1809789f3" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049312 :topic/id #uuid "eb826c2f-ae04-5de5-b6a6-7efcf7e974ae" :topic/math-academy-id 2201} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427637 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "045918a8-9cd8-5a07-b550-ae46024d9091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415446} {:answer/id #uuid "402ee237-56af-5ed0-b68b-15a4eb93a4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415451} {:answer/id #uuid "82c9a685-f3be-5652-9e92-444a23e21632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415458} {:answer/id #uuid "f5705fa2-288d-561a-9ae0-435e05884593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} {:answer/id #uuid "fff98d8e-e1e9-59ce-9f45-62d4096f2b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415469}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} :answer-field/id #uuid "3898e8c8-305f-5107-8e55-3fa0057b225c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "135c5d03-e391-5a5b-8227-7d54c7203318" :question/math-academy-id "q-140048" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n|A|=0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0=0\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"} :step/id #uuid "1a88a749-d24f-53f0-b27d-bb6b30fd5b09"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427638 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329653 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25ffab26-9ad7-506d-a32e-290001bd0683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327263} {:answer/id #uuid "8218f764-70b6-55d4-8b25-1cd4c71771d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328055} {:answer/id #uuid "ba930e46-114f-5ca4-bd55-ff9ff7367bb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328559} {:answer/id #uuid "c30c03d6-9daa-5660-bfd1-f61e521c01ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328638} {:answer/id #uuid "ed725a19-ce5e-5e0d-bc81-259288441adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329013}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329013} :answer-field/id #uuid "357d9d24-cb3b-5a09-9abd-87033d967adf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "59d4edee-acd9-59e0-80f8-ec390e2e0ee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42465" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{6} & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nI. $A$ has proportional rows\n\nII. $A$ has identical columns\n\nIII. $A$ has a zero column" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{6} & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have a zero column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :step/id #uuid "388fa099-949a-55ed-903a-cb5e3105da1f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427639}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427639 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba7d7bc9-77ef-583c-8caa-22315aad7aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$, $|B|$, and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392523} {:answer/id #uuid "23f02ed7-eb83-5988-a1ca-ee80eac659ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392524} {:answer/id #uuid "d767aec8-a44c-5175-bbcd-b71f577015fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392525} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7ae539-44fc-5d03-b8b9-5a5b498db62e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392526} {:answer/id #uuid "3737a2a5-a57d-571a-a651-f2cad4ee3049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392527}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392525} :answer-field/id #uuid "00ef10bc-f305-5726-8271-949923025e38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cee2c526-7176-535a-81f7-173bfaefecec" :question/math-academy-id "q-42882" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=1\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=12\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"} :step/id #uuid "38a574a5-5c5f-57c3-888b-5d032802d120" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427640}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427640 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d8e0b89-42bf-519d-9d97-5be58994dc91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327337} {:answer/id #uuid "43e90ae2-41ae-5a8b-bd0d-a84be897dc3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327526} {:answer/id #uuid "cd965883-d1dd-572c-b5e0-9d1d81b810b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328742} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d7cf84-3b4e-527a-beaf-e866d3ca0aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328938} {:answer/id #uuid "f499f0e7-80e6-54c9-b9ec-b1cb786a0558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329076}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327337} :answer-field/id #uuid "73a52cef-1ba2-5963-a084-9155ceff6344" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ef67ff18-5c70-5c00-bdf0-27b79dc90b72" :question/math-academy-id "q-43306" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nI. $A$ has two identical rows\n\nII. One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n\nIII. $A$ has two identical columns" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=1\\cdot 8-4\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor two identical columns.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} :step/id #uuid "9758fa31-2a83-569c-bfa7-a2c551b1e63f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427641}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427641 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427636 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c03a16b-9dee-5cff-a0ff-6bb3df36fd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427630} {:answer/id #uuid "317dd47a-723e-5f7b-bb84-76a98d476a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427631} {:answer/id #uuid "51f27d1e-2a2e-57fb-a28c-b54b35283c0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427632} {:answer/id #uuid "a64fab7a-ae4b-5ae6-9ea8-75c59aee1472" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427633} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ae2b06-54e1-5537-a7a1-e4af212bb060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427634}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427630} :answer-field/id #uuid "25bbbab1-f79f-5a4a-95b4-1d90cbb77585" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "df55035e-2530-507b-9e8e-793ed8f0bafc" :question/math-academy-id "q-82284" :question/problem "Find $-4det(A)+3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\ndet(B)=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3=6\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-4det(A)+3det(B)=-4\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 6=18.$"} :step/id #uuid "f880731a-4b09-56ca-8e32-d2d537e03030" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427637}}] :activity/title "Conditions When a Determinant Equals Zero" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427629}]}
